## Why This Is Asked
Real-time trading platforms demand ultra-low latency combined with robust replay protection across distributed microservices. Token binding mechanisms reduce impersonation risks while maintaining performance requirements critical to trading operations.

## Key Concepts
- Token binding and mutual TLS (mTLS) for connection-specific authentication
- Short time-to-live (TTL) tokens with audience-scoping for service isolation
- WebSocket connection nonces and replay prevention mechanisms
- Global revocation propagation strategies
- Comprehensive observability and audit trail implementation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate token and bind to nonce
function authorize(token, nonce, ctx){
  if (!isValidToken(token)) return false;
  if (!bindsToTLS(token, ctx)) return false;
  const session = createSecureSession(token, nonce);
  return session.isValid() && !isReplayAttempt(nonce);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This scenario evaluates your ability to design practical security measures that address API key compromise while maintaining system usability. It tests understanding of token-based authentication, device security, and implementation strategies that balance security with operational feasibility.

## Key Concepts

- Per-device tokens versus global API keys for granular access control
- PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange) for secure mobile/SPA authentication flows
- Device fingerprint binding to prevent token reuse across unauthorized devices
- Token binding at API gateway level for additional security layers
- Short token lifetimes with secure refresh token rotation mechanisms
- Per-token rate limiting and behavioral anomaly detection for abuse prevention
- Phased migration approaches to minimize user disruption

## Code Example

```javascript
// Node.js: verify per-device JWT binding
const verifyDeviceToken = (token, deviceFingerprint) => {
  const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
  if (decoded.deviceFingerprint !== deviceFingerprint) {
    throw new Error('Token-device mismatch');
  }
  return decoded;
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design runtime policy enforcement for multi-tenant data access, addressing drift, performance, and rollback.

## Key Concepts

